The upstream files retain their copyright and license headers. Locally archived
snapshots normalize text line endings to LF. Extracted kernels retain function
bodies and triton.jit decorators; FlagGems dispatch/autotune decorators are
omitted. GELU's math helpers are bound to the Ascend shims used by the historical
experiment. Where/GELU use an explicitly identified continuous pointwise adapter.
Baseline and manual variants change launch tile/grid parameters, not formulas.

The repository's test harness, documentation and data organization are provided
under the same Apache-2.0 license. Historical benchmark results describe only
their recorded configurations and hardware, and do not imply upstream endorsement.
